From 4c31e05ff16091e63b3c88f36d38060b757c3f7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:31:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: one holdsTurnClaim(state) predicate for
 busy/awaiting/turnLive

PR #1913 fixed a bug where the "holds a turn claim" predicate
(busy || awaitingResponse || turnLive) drifted between its hand-written
copies. Give it one home: holdsTurnClaim() in session-states-live-turn.ts,
next to isLiveTurnAwaitingEvents (moved there too and now built on it),
both re-exported from session-states.

Call sites now using it: reconcileBusyStatesOnReconnect (both checks),
the tile delegate's retireBusyClaim, the reconnect test's delegate
mirror, and native-notifications' deferred-completion retry.

No behaviour change. session-states.ts is net -2 lines.

Follow-up to review t_01a1d38ee5c6a455 of PR #1913 (card t_01a1d392801b804e).
